1
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:04,010
The next section of the female genital tract

2
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:06,490
that we're gonna cover is the endometrium and the myometrium.

3
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:10,030
Basically, both of these make up the uterine wall.

4
00:00:10,470 --> 00:00:13,010
Remember that the endometrium is the mucosal lining

5
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:16,250
of the uterine cavity, and the myometrium is that smooth muscle

6
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,790
that underlies the endometrium.

7
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:20,750
Here's a histologic picture, just to remind you of normal.

8
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:23,650
So again, we're gonna make a little division here,

9
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:26,590
and we're gonna remind ourselves that this is the endometrium,

10
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:29,570
and that's the mucosa that lines the uterine cavity,

11
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,790
and then this is the myometrium, and of course,

12
00:00:32,890 --> 00:00:35,070
the myometrium, as you'll recall from histology,

13
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:36,730
is made up of smooth muscle.

14
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:39,450
Now, remember from physiology that the endometrium

15
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:41,990
is hormonally sensitive, and it grows with estrogen,

16
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:44,470
and then gets prepared with progesterone,

17
00:00:44,610 --> 00:00:47,170
and then sheds when you remove the progesterone support.

18
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:49,350
So we wanted to remind ourselves of that.

19
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:51,470
We would just remember that it grows,

20
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:59,660
and then it's prepared, and then it sheds.

21
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:05,470
So remember that there is a proliferative phase

22
00:01:05,470 --> 00:01:07,910
during which it grows, and this is driven by estrogen,

23
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:12,690
and then there is a secretory phase

24
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:14,410
in which it is prepared for implantation,

25
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:16,250
and this occurs via progesterone,

26
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:20,690
and then eventually, when there's loss of progesterone support,

27
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:23,170
we get shedding, and shedding occurs,

28
00:01:23,330 --> 00:01:25,270
and that results in menstruation.

29
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:27,870
All right, first syndrome that we want to discuss,

30
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:28,750
Asherman syndrome.

31
00:01:29,190 --> 00:01:33,330
Now, the idea here is that the patients get secondary amenorrhea,

32
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:36,590
and the reason they get secondary amenorrhea is because

33
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:38,470
they lose their basalis,

34
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:41,690
which is the regenerative layer of the endometrium.

35
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:44,930
Now, this requires us to go back a step and remind ourselves

36
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:46,910
that when you look at the endometrium histologically,

37
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:50,150
and when you understand the endometrium physiologically,

38
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:53,590
remember that the endometrium grows and produces a functional layer

39
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:55,990
called a functionalis, and then that sheds,

40
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:58,750
and then it grows again and produces a new functionalis,

41
00:01:58,830 --> 00:02:00,770
and then that sheds, and then it grows again,

42
00:02:00,770 --> 00:02:01,850
and then sheds, et cetera.

43
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:06,770
Now, the layer that regenerates that endometrium with each cycle,

44
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:08,610
that's called the basalis.

45
00:02:09,410 --> 00:02:12,470
So the basalis is the regenerative layer of the endometrium.

46
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:14,790
It is the stem cells of the endometrium,

47
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:16,890
and by the way, examiners love to ask you

48
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:19,170
where the stem cells are in particular disorders.

49
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:21,870
Now, imagine if we had a circumstance

50
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:23,950
in which we lost that basalis.

51
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:25,710
If we lost the basalis,

52
00:02:25,810 --> 00:02:27,890
we wouldn't be able to regenerate the endometrium,

53
00:02:28,270 --> 00:02:30,210
and if we couldn't regenerate the endometrium,

54
00:02:30,210 --> 00:02:32,990
the endometrium of the patients would then get secondary amenorrhea,

55
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:36,250
which would be, you know, a lack of menstrual cycles.

56
00:02:36,890 --> 00:02:39,230
Now, what would be the cause of Asherman syndrome

57
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:41,990
in this secondary amenorrhea with loss of the basalis?

58
00:02:42,510 --> 00:02:46,190
Well, a common cause is overaggressive DNC.

59
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:48,830
Now, in a DNC, what happens is,

60
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:50,710
let's say a patient needs a DNC,

61
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:53,190
and we want to go in there and scrape something out of the uterus.

62
00:02:53,570 --> 00:02:55,990
Well, we go in there, literally, we dilate the cervix,

63
00:02:55,990 --> 00:03:00,750
and then we curatage or scrape away the surface of the uterine wall.

64
00:03:01,050 --> 00:03:04,290
Now, imagine if the physician or the person performing the procedure

65
00:03:04,290 --> 00:03:07,810
is too aggressive in that scraping away of the uterine wall.

66
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:09,670
They could actually scrape away the basalis,

67
00:03:10,090 --> 00:03:11,410
and if you knock out the basalis,

68
00:03:11,770 --> 00:03:15,150
there is not going to be the ability to regenerate that endometrium,

69
00:03:15,510 --> 00:03:18,230
and therefore, the patients will get secondary amenorrhea.

70
00:03:18,230 --> 00:03:22,410
So, that is a rare but possible complication of DNC,

71
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:24,230
and that's called Asherman syndrome.

72
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:25,610
Again, what's the high yield here?

73
00:03:25,990 --> 00:03:27,850
The whole notion of the basalis.

74
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:31,490
That's what's important when understanding the principle of this disease.

75
00:03:32,230 --> 00:03:34,250
The next disorder that we're going to talk about

76
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:35,810
is called anovulatory cycle.

77
00:03:36,370 --> 00:03:37,570
Now, in this particular case,

78
00:03:37,630 --> 00:03:40,370
what happens is the patient goes through a proliferative phase,

79
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:42,130
but they don't ovulate,

80
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:44,050
and remember that once ovulation occurs,

81
00:03:44,050 --> 00:03:49,210
that then puts us into the secretory phase of the endometrial cycle

82
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:52,010
where we prepare the endometrium with progesterone.

83
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:55,930
And so, in an anovulatory cycle,

84
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:57,710
there is a lack of ovulation.

85
00:03:57,970 --> 00:04:03,670
That lack of ovulation results in a lack of a progesterone-driven secretory phase,

86
00:04:03,990 --> 00:04:06,050
and then eventually, the patients present with bleeding.

87
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,470
And so, the idea here is that you've got estrogen.

88
00:04:08,630 --> 00:04:10,110
It causes the endometrium to grow,

89
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:12,270
and then you're supposed to have progesterone,

90
00:04:12,270 --> 00:04:13,610
which will prepare the endometrium,

91
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:15,410
and then eventually, when it's withdrawn,

92
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:16,870
will make the endometrium shed.

93
00:04:17,270 --> 00:04:18,310
But in this particular case,

94
00:04:18,370 --> 00:04:20,730
the patient has estrogen, and the endometrium grows,

95
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:23,270
and then they don't undergo the progesterone phase.

96
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:25,710
Now, when they continue with their cycle,

97
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:27,870
they're again going to get another estrogen phase,

98
00:04:27,930 --> 00:04:29,930
which is going to cause growth of the endometrium

99
00:04:29,930 --> 00:04:31,770
on top of the previous growth,

100
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:35,430
which then eventually will result in overgrowth of the blood supply.

101
00:04:35,810 --> 00:04:37,750
So, the cells will grow beyond the blood supply,

102
00:04:38,070 --> 00:04:40,870
and they'll begin to degenerate,

103
00:04:40,870 --> 00:04:42,590
and eventually, there'll be some bleeding.

104
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:45,350
So, that results in dysfunctional uterine bleeding.

105
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:49,550
Now, classically, an anovulatory cycle is seen during menarche

106
00:04:49,550 --> 00:04:51,010
and during menopause.

107
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:52,830
And so, those are the classic times

108
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:55,210
when there can be abnormalities in bleeding,

109
00:04:55,390 --> 00:05:00,810
and there can be irregular bleeding due to an anovulatory cycle.

110
00:05:01,990 --> 00:05:05,510
Acute endometritis refers to infection of the endometrium.

111
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:06,470
It's usually bacterial.

112
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:09,970
One of the common causes is retained products of conception.

113
00:05:09,970 --> 00:05:13,010
So, we deliver the baby, then we deliver the placenta,

114
00:05:13,190 --> 00:05:15,730
and let's say a piece of the placenta remains behind.

115
00:05:16,130 --> 00:05:19,750
So, that could become a nidus for a bacterial infection,

116
00:05:20,030 --> 00:05:22,010
which would then result in acute endometritis.

117
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,010
The patients will present with fever,

118
00:05:24,670 --> 00:05:27,130
abnormal uterine bleeding, and pelvic pain.

119
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:30,110
So, these are the classic symptoms, and they all make sense,

120
00:05:30,170 --> 00:05:33,370
because basically, you have inflammation of the uterine body.

121
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:35,370
And when you have inflammation of the uterine body,

122
00:05:35,450 --> 00:05:37,490
there's going to be pelvic pain.

123
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:39,070
And then, of course, there's infection,

124
00:05:39,210 --> 00:05:39,990
so there'll be fever,

125
00:05:40,350 --> 00:05:42,070
and then there'll be some bleeding as well.

126
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:44,550
So, these are the key symptoms of acute endometritis.

127
00:05:45,270 --> 00:05:47,510
Chronic endometritis is when you have chronic inflammation

128
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:48,370
of the endometrium.

129
00:05:48,590 --> 00:05:50,010
What's important to note here

130
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:53,450
is that lymphocytes are normally present in the endometrium.

131
00:05:53,450 --> 00:05:55,750
They can be seen in the endometrium,

132
00:05:56,150 --> 00:05:59,090
and therefore, the characteristic cell is a plasma cell.

133
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:02,510
So, you actually have to see a plasma cell in the endometrium

134
00:06:02,510 --> 00:06:04,450
in order to call chronic endometritis.

135
00:06:05,190 --> 00:06:08,370
So, it's a histologic diagnosis.

136
00:06:09,110 --> 00:06:11,410
Common causes include retained products of conception,

137
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:14,270
chronic pelvic inflammatory disease,

138
00:06:14,390 --> 00:06:16,150
especially chlamydia, for example,

139
00:06:16,530 --> 00:06:17,910
can give you a chronic endometritis.

140
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:22,070
An intrauterine device can become secondarily infected

141
00:06:22,070 --> 00:06:23,970
and give chronic endometritis.

142
00:06:25,230 --> 00:06:27,190
TB would give you chronic endometritis,

143
00:06:27,350 --> 00:06:28,750
and in that particular case, of course,

144
00:06:28,810 --> 00:06:29,890
we would see granulomas,

145
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:32,270
so we would get granulomas with TB.

146
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:33,870
I think we're all well aware of that.

147
00:06:34,370 --> 00:06:36,470
These patients, they present with abnormal uterine bleeding,

148
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:37,830
pelvic pain, and infertility.

149
00:06:37,910 --> 00:06:38,890
And infertility is important,

150
00:06:38,990 --> 00:06:40,810
because I'll tell you that it's common

151
00:06:40,810 --> 00:06:43,150
for endometrial biopsies to be done

152
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:44,350
in patients with infertility,

153
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:46,590
and they'll write on the requisition

154
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:48,390
when they submit that biopsy,

155
00:06:48,890 --> 00:06:51,090
please check for chronic endometritis.

156
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:52,450
And when they say that,

157
00:06:52,530 --> 00:06:54,570
I know that I need to now look for plasma cells

158
00:06:54,570 --> 00:06:55,650
in the endometrium,

159
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:57,410
because this patient has infertility,

160
00:06:57,510 --> 00:06:58,550
and they're trying to determine

161
00:06:58,550 --> 00:07:00,570
whether chronic endometritis might be

162
00:07:00,570 --> 00:07:02,270
a cause of that infertility.

163
00:07:03,270 --> 00:07:05,290
The next disorder, endometrial polyp.

164
00:07:05,810 --> 00:07:09,130
Endometrial polyp is a hyperplastic protrusion

165
00:07:09,130 --> 00:07:10,050
of endometrium.

166
00:07:10,450 --> 00:07:12,050
It presents with abnormal uterine bleeding.

167
00:07:12,050 --> 00:07:14,590
The idea here, this is the endometrial polyp.

168
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:16,590
This is the surface of the endometrium here,

169
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:17,910
but you can clearly see

170
00:07:17,910 --> 00:07:19,650
that we've developed this big polyp.

171
00:07:19,970 --> 00:07:21,570
Now, obviously, as this polyp begins

172
00:07:21,570 --> 00:07:23,130
to stretch away at the endometrium,

173
00:07:23,390 --> 00:07:24,690
that's going to result in bleeding.

174
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:27,130
And so the classic presenting sign

175
00:07:27,130 --> 00:07:30,090
of an endometrial polyp is abnormal uterine bleeding.

176
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:32,610
Now, one very important high-yield

177
00:07:32,610 --> 00:07:34,030
pharma association here

178
00:07:34,030 --> 00:07:36,190
is that the patients can actually develop

179
00:07:36,190 --> 00:07:38,670
endometrial polyps as a side effect of tamoxifen.

180
00:07:39,070 --> 00:07:40,370
A little bit counterintuitive,

181
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:42,550
because when you think about tamoxifen,

182
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:45,090
you think about its anti-estrogenic effects,

183
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:46,230
especially in the breast.

184
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:48,590
However, it's important to note

185
00:07:48,590 --> 00:07:51,870
that tamoxifen is actually anti-estrogenic

186
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:52,590
on the breast,

187
00:07:52,830 --> 00:07:55,530
but it has weak pro-estrogenic effects

188
00:07:55,530 --> 00:07:56,470
on the endometrium.

189
00:07:56,790 --> 00:07:58,570
And it's those pro-estrogenic effects

190
00:07:58,570 --> 00:08:01,030
of tamoxifen that result in the production

191
00:08:01,030 --> 00:08:02,770
of an endometrial polyp.

192
00:08:03,590 --> 00:08:05,010
This is, again, the picture

193
00:08:05,010 --> 00:08:06,110
of the endometrial polyp,

194
00:08:06,150 --> 00:08:07,110
which I've already explained

195
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:08,470
and is present in your text.

196
00:08:09,570 --> 00:08:11,930
The next disorder in the text, endometriosis.

197
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:13,570
What is endometriosis?

198
00:08:13,770 --> 00:08:16,290
It is the abnormal placement

199
00:08:16,290 --> 00:08:20,430
of both endometrial glands and stroma

200
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,450
outside of the uterine cavity.

201
00:08:23,810 --> 00:08:25,830
Endometrial glands and stroma,

202
00:08:26,110 --> 00:08:27,390
and I should actually be more correct

203
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:29,850
in saying outside of the endometrial lining.

204
00:08:30,490 --> 00:08:31,970
So when endometrial glands and stroma

205
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:34,570
are misplaced in another location,

206
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:36,410
that's called endometriosis.

207
00:08:36,830 --> 00:08:38,710
Now, I keep emphasizing this,

208
00:08:38,850 --> 00:08:40,950
endometrial glands and stroma.

209
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:41,610
It's both.

210
00:08:41,670 --> 00:08:43,950
It's both the glands and the stroma

211
00:08:43,950 --> 00:08:46,350
of the endometrium that would be misplaced.

212
00:08:46,930 --> 00:08:48,710
This is going to present with dysmenorrhea,

213
00:08:48,850 --> 00:08:51,390
which is pain during the menstrual cycle.

214
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:52,730
And the reason is because

215
00:08:52,730 --> 00:08:54,490
these displaced glands and stroma

216
00:08:54,490 --> 00:08:56,610
are going to cycle the same way

217
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:57,870
that the endometrium would cycle.

218
00:08:58,270 --> 00:08:59,690
And so that can result in pain,

219
00:08:59,690 --> 00:09:01,870
particularly because this tissue is located

220
00:09:01,870 --> 00:09:04,030
in an abnormal location.

221
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:06,610
So there'll be dysmenorrhea and pelvic pain.

222
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:09,930
Infertility can also be a consequence

223
00:09:09,930 --> 00:09:12,990
of endometriosis, as I'm going to make clear

224
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:14,810
as we move forward in our discussion.

225
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:18,430
So one more thing that I should remind you of,

226
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:20,670
and sometimes examiners like to ask,

227
00:09:20,970 --> 00:09:23,950
so what do we believe currently causes endometriosis?

228
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:26,710
Well, there's actually three distinct theories

229
00:09:26,710 --> 00:09:30,190
of how endometriosis develops.

230
00:09:30,870 --> 00:09:32,610
The first of those theories is called

231
00:09:32,610 --> 00:09:34,690
the retrograde menstruation theory.

232
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:37,290
And the idea here is that some menstrual products

233
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:39,050
go backward instead of out,

234
00:09:39,290 --> 00:09:40,750
and they go up through the tubes

235
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:42,430
and then eventually can go into the ovary

236
00:09:42,430 --> 00:09:43,890
and can eventually go into the pelvis.

237
00:09:44,390 --> 00:09:46,110
So that's called the retrograde theory.

238
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:47,270
And that's one way,

239
00:09:47,430 --> 00:09:49,270
and that's sort of the leading theory at this point

240
00:09:49,270 --> 00:09:52,470
as to how endometriosis develops.

241
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:55,530
The next of the theories is the metaplastic theory.

242
00:09:55,530 --> 00:09:57,570
And the idea behind the metaplastic theory

243
00:09:57,570 --> 00:10:00,530
is that the malarian duct

244
00:10:00,530 --> 00:10:04,270
from which the uterine wall, et cetera, develops,

245
00:10:04,650 --> 00:10:06,350
it has the ability to develop

246
00:10:06,350 --> 00:10:08,830
into multiple different types of epithelium.

247
00:10:08,930 --> 00:10:09,510
So for example,

248
00:10:09,890 --> 00:10:12,550
the cervical epithelium develops from the malarian duct.

249
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:14,470
The endometrial epithelium develops

250
00:10:14,470 --> 00:10:16,030
from the malarian duct, et cetera.

251
00:10:16,470 --> 00:10:18,550
And so there's a metaplastic theory

252
00:10:18,550 --> 00:10:20,530
in which it's believed that there's metaplasia

253
00:10:21,190 --> 00:10:23,530
or endometrial metaplasia of some of the epithelium,

254
00:10:23,530 --> 00:10:25,850
which then results in endometriosis.

255
00:10:26,510 --> 00:10:27,530
And there's a third theory

256
00:10:28,130 --> 00:10:29,790
which basically is called

257
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:32,130
the lymphatic dissemination theory.

258
00:10:32,450 --> 00:10:34,370
And the idea here is that the endometriosis

259
00:10:34,370 --> 00:10:35,570
goes through the lymphatics

260
00:10:35,570 --> 00:10:38,670
and then begins to spread to other regions.

261
00:10:38,910 --> 00:10:40,850
And the people who argue for that theory,

262
00:10:41,050 --> 00:10:43,770
they argue that it's possible to see endometriosis

263
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:44,950
in very strange sites,

264
00:10:45,070 --> 00:10:46,170
like for example, the lung.

265
00:10:46,470 --> 00:10:48,170
So how would endometriosis get to the lung?

266
00:10:48,170 --> 00:10:49,490
It must go through the lymphatics.

267
00:10:49,630 --> 00:10:50,690
It can't be retrograde

268
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:52,850
because retrograde would not give you access to the lung.

269
00:10:53,350 --> 00:10:54,950
Anyway, that's a little bit of theoretical.

270
00:10:55,430 --> 00:10:56,650
What's probably most important

271
00:10:56,650 --> 00:11:00,590
is to recognize that the current prevailing theory

272
00:11:00,590 --> 00:11:03,430
is the retrograde menstruation theory.

273
00:11:03,990 --> 00:11:05,250
When you have endometriosis,

274
00:11:05,250 --> 00:11:06,910
there are some common sites of involvement.

275
00:11:07,110 --> 00:11:09,730
The most common site of involvement is the ovary.

276
00:11:10,130 --> 00:11:12,210
And the classic problem within the ovary

277
00:11:12,210 --> 00:11:13,530
is called the chocolate cyst.

278
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:15,570
And I'll illustrate that in a few minutes

279
00:11:15,570 --> 00:11:16,790
when we get to the next slide.

280
00:11:17,330 --> 00:11:19,130
Other places where you can have involvement,

281
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,790
you can have involvement of the uterine ligaments,

282
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:22,050
which would cause pelvic pain,

283
00:11:22,490 --> 00:11:23,850
involvement of the pouch of Douglas,

284
00:11:24,150 --> 00:11:25,730
which would give pain with defecation,

285
00:11:26,150 --> 00:11:27,150
the bladder wall,

286
00:11:27,310 --> 00:11:28,630
which would give pain with urination,

287
00:11:29,130 --> 00:11:30,270
the cirrhosis of the bowel,

288
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:31,950
abdominal pain and adhesions,

289
00:11:31,950 --> 00:11:34,850
and the fallopian tube can result in scarring.

290
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:36,930
Now, if you involve the fallopian tube

291
00:11:36,930 --> 00:11:37,830
with endometriosis,

292
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:41,650
you're going to get some damage and some scarring.

293
00:11:41,770 --> 00:11:45,190
And that scarring could then prohibit the egg

294
00:11:45,190 --> 00:11:46,290
from reaching the,

295
00:11:46,450 --> 00:11:49,630
from being able to move to the uterine cavity.

296
00:11:50,050 --> 00:11:52,710
And so that's going to increase the risk of infertility.

297
00:11:52,930 --> 00:11:55,270
And it's also going to increase the risk

298
00:11:55,270 --> 00:11:57,510
of ectopic tubal pregnancy,

299
00:11:57,790 --> 00:12:01,890
i.e. the implantation of the ovum into,

300
00:12:02,030 --> 00:12:04,050
the fertilized ovum into a place

301
00:12:04,050 --> 00:12:06,090
other than the uterine wall.

302
00:12:06,590 --> 00:12:07,910
So these are common sites of involvement.

303
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:09,110
These are some of the complications.

304
00:12:09,610 --> 00:12:12,090
I think if you understand a little bit of basic anatomy,

305
00:12:12,090 --> 00:12:13,670
it's not hard to understand

306
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:15,550
these classic signs and symptoms.

307
00:12:16,050 --> 00:12:20,770
Again, chocolate cysts being the most important of these

308
00:12:20,770 --> 00:12:23,090
and fallopian tube scarring

309
00:12:23,090 --> 00:12:25,270
with the subsequent risk for both infertility

310
00:12:25,270 --> 00:12:28,450
and for ectopic tubal pregnancy

311
00:12:28,450 --> 00:12:30,870
being the second most important on this list.

312
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:33,330
Now, here's a picture of a chocolate cyst.

313
00:12:33,830 --> 00:12:35,730
This entire thing is the ovary.

314
00:12:36,050 --> 00:12:37,050
And you can clearly see

315
00:12:37,050 --> 00:12:39,190
that there's a cystic lesion within the ovary.

316
00:12:39,190 --> 00:12:42,810
And this cystic lesion is full of this chocolate bloody material.

317
00:12:43,010 --> 00:12:44,810
This is just menstrual products, basically,

318
00:12:45,230 --> 00:12:47,090
which then accumulates as a cyst.

319
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,670
So this is called the chocolate cyst of the ovary.

320
00:12:50,010 --> 00:12:51,130
Again, let's remind ourselves

321
00:12:51,130 --> 00:12:52,550
that if we've got a normal ovary

322
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:55,330
and we get a little bit of endometriosis that implants,

323
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:56,750
what's going to happen is

324
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:58,810
the endometrium is going to grow and shed

325
00:12:58,810 --> 00:13:01,190
and grow and shed and grow and shed

326
00:13:01,190 --> 00:13:03,170
and grow and shed with each subsequent cycle.

327
00:13:03,510 --> 00:13:04,970
And that's going to result in the accumulation

328
00:13:04,970 --> 00:13:06,690
of all this bloody debris,

329
00:13:06,690 --> 00:13:09,550
which then is going to produce that chocolate cyst.

330
00:13:09,990 --> 00:13:11,450
So that's the basic theory there.

331
00:13:11,710 --> 00:13:12,770
Now, here's another picture.

332
00:13:12,930 --> 00:13:16,550
This is involvement of soft tissues by the endometriosis.

333
00:13:17,010 --> 00:13:18,210
And the idea here is that

334
00:13:18,210 --> 00:13:20,410
we've got all these little brown specks.

335
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:23,530
These are also called gunpowder lesions.

336
00:13:24,090 --> 00:13:26,410
And this is what endometriosis looks like

337
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:27,870
when it involves soft tissue.

338
00:13:27,970 --> 00:13:30,910
It produces these little hemorrhagic areas,

339
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:32,390
these little brown hemorrhagic areas,

340
00:13:32,470 --> 00:13:34,410
which are also called gunpowder lesions.

341
00:13:34,410 --> 00:13:35,890
And you need to be familiar with that

342
00:13:35,890 --> 00:13:37,950
for examination purposes as well.

343
00:13:38,490 --> 00:13:40,690
Now, one very high yield principle to recognize

344
00:13:40,690 --> 00:13:42,750
is that you can actually get endometriosis

345
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:44,570
that involves the myometrium.

346
00:13:45,030 --> 00:13:46,970
So remember that you've got the endometrium up here

347
00:13:46,970 --> 00:13:48,510
and then you've got the myometrium here.

348
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:50,790
If you get endometrial glands and stroma

349
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:53,090
that are actually present within the myometrium,

350
00:13:53,610 --> 00:13:55,990
that's endometriosis of the myometrium.

351
00:13:56,230 --> 00:13:57,570
That gets a special name

352
00:13:57,570 --> 00:13:59,110
and that's called adenomyosis.

353
00:13:59,110 --> 00:14:01,910
And you can bet that that term shows up on exams.

354
00:14:03,130 --> 00:14:07,130
Adenomyosis is the presence of endometriosis

355
00:14:07,130 --> 00:14:09,430
within the myometrium.

356
00:14:09,790 --> 00:14:12,050
The adeno here refers to the endometrial glands

357
00:14:12,050 --> 00:14:15,610
and the myo refers to the fact that it's in the muscle.

358
00:14:16,050 --> 00:14:17,510
So adenomyosis.

359
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:18,770
You need to know that term.

360
00:14:19,670 --> 00:14:21,610
One of the complications of endometriosis

361
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:23,350
along with the clinical signs and symptoms

362
00:14:23,350 --> 00:14:25,830
is that there is an increased risk for carcinoma

363
00:14:25,830 --> 00:14:29,190
at the site of endometriosis, especially the ovary.

364
00:14:29,650 --> 00:14:31,790
And this is going to come back a little later

365
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:32,490
in our discussion,

366
00:14:32,730 --> 00:14:35,090
so it's nice to bury this away in our minds now.

367
00:14:35,390 --> 00:14:36,830
An increased risk of carcinoma

368
00:14:36,830 --> 00:14:38,170
at the site of endometriosis,

369
00:14:38,410 --> 00:14:40,630
especially when it involves the ovary.

370
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:43,950
Another lesion to be familiar with in the endometrium

371
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:45,950
is called endometrial hyperplasia.

372
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:48,730
This is hyperplasia of the endometrial glands

373
00:14:48,730 --> 00:14:50,110
relative to the stroma.

374
00:14:50,450 --> 00:14:51,350
Let's illustrate this.

375
00:14:51,410 --> 00:14:53,330
Let's pretend that we're looking at this on a slide.

376
00:14:53,770 --> 00:14:54,970
Now you'll recognize that when you look

377
00:14:54,970 --> 00:14:55,870
at a piece of endometrium,

378
00:14:55,990 --> 00:14:57,510
you might see some glands,

379
00:14:57,630 --> 00:14:58,950
like here and here and here,

380
00:14:59,350 --> 00:15:01,870
and then the rest of what is present as white,

381
00:15:01,990 --> 00:15:04,170
all of this would actually represent stroma.

382
00:15:04,910 --> 00:15:06,330
This is the connective tissue

383
00:15:06,330 --> 00:15:07,870
that holds together the endometrium.

384
00:15:08,330 --> 00:15:10,490
And so normally you see a certain number of glands,

385
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:13,050
and then you see the endometrial stroma

386
00:15:13,050 --> 00:15:14,510
associated with those glands.

387
00:15:14,890 --> 00:15:16,790
What happens in endometrial hyperplasia

388
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:17,950
is the following.

389
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:21,030
You're going to have a slide, for example,

390
00:15:21,210 --> 00:15:22,790
which is just showing you the relationship

391
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:23,970
of the glands to the stroma,

392
00:15:23,970 --> 00:15:27,270
and instead of having glands and stroma equally spaced out,

393
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,790
you start getting a lot of glands relative to the stroma.

394
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:34,010
And that is what defines endometrial hyperplasia.

395
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:35,990
And that's why I say in your book here

396
00:15:35,990 --> 00:15:38,930
that it is a hyperplasia of the endometrial glands

397
00:15:38,930 --> 00:15:40,110
relative to the stroma.

398
00:15:40,490 --> 00:15:41,670
What drives this process?

399
00:15:41,950 --> 00:15:43,330
Estrogen, estrogen, estrogen.

400
00:15:43,330 --> 00:15:47,090
This is a consequence of unopposed estrogen.

401
00:15:47,610 --> 00:15:49,370
So if a patient's got unopposed estrogen,

402
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:52,670
meaning estrogen that's not followed by a progesterone phase,

403
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:54,490
they develop endometrial hyperplasia.

404
00:15:54,770 --> 00:15:57,150
So it's classically seen in a postmenopausal woman

405
00:15:57,150 --> 00:16:00,190
because they would have stopped their progesterone phase

406
00:16:00,190 --> 00:16:01,610
because they're no longer menstruating,

407
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:03,590
but they still are seeing some estrogen.

408
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:05,330
For example, let's say she's obese.

409
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:09,390
And in obesity, we know that androgen gets converted to estrone,

410
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:12,690
a estrogen, which is called estrone, in the fat.

411
00:16:12,810 --> 00:16:15,470
So adipose tissue can convert androgen to estrone.

412
00:16:15,830 --> 00:16:18,490
That peripheral conversion to estrone

413
00:16:18,490 --> 00:16:20,110
will then hit the endometrium

414
00:16:20,110 --> 00:16:22,830
and cause the endometrium to undergo a hyperplasia.

415
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:24,850
So that's one of the classic examples

416
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:27,830
in which a patient might have endometrial hyperplasia.

417
00:16:28,450 --> 00:16:29,390
Now how does it present?

418
00:16:29,490 --> 00:16:31,810
It presents as postmenopausal uterine bleeding.

419
00:16:31,810 --> 00:16:35,350
So as the endometrium begins to grow and grow and grow and grow,

420
00:16:35,690 --> 00:16:36,770
it'll eventually bleed.

421
00:16:37,050 --> 00:16:39,710
And when it bleeds, that's the way by which the patients present.

422
00:16:40,410 --> 00:16:43,850
Here's a classic image of endometrial hyperplasia.

423
00:16:44,110 --> 00:16:45,690
So these are all endometrial glands.

424
00:16:45,970 --> 00:16:48,670
And normally the endometrial glands should not be so crowded.

425
00:16:48,830 --> 00:16:51,290
They should not be on top of each other the way they are here,

426
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:53,130
just sort of back to back to back almost.

427
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:56,610
And so this is an example of endometrial hyperplasia.

428
00:16:57,170 --> 00:16:59,750
Important to note, again, for examination purposes

429
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:02,610
and for when you're trying to deal with the pathologist

430
00:17:02,610 --> 00:17:04,650
when you're working in the clinics,

431
00:17:05,030 --> 00:17:06,610
that we classify this histologically.

432
00:17:07,030 --> 00:17:09,190
Remember that we classify endometrial hyperplasia

433
00:17:09,190 --> 00:17:10,230
based on architecture.

434
00:17:10,590 --> 00:17:14,190
And if you recall, in architecture we talk about simple and complex.

435
00:17:14,430 --> 00:17:15,830
So we can have simple hyperplasia

436
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:17,490
and we can have complex hyperplasia.

437
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:21,750
At the same time, we also classify it based on nuclear or cellular atypia.

438
00:17:22,170 --> 00:17:25,890
And so we can say simple hyperplasia with or without atypia

439
00:17:25,890 --> 00:17:28,950
and complex hyperplasia with or without atypia.

440
00:17:29,370 --> 00:17:30,950
There's a high-yield examiner's question

441
00:17:30,950 --> 00:17:32,610
that shows up on most examinations,

442
00:17:32,730 --> 00:17:35,770
whether it be medical school examinations or board examinations,

443
00:17:36,170 --> 00:17:37,330
and that is the following,

444
00:17:37,450 --> 00:17:40,230
that the most important predictor for progression to cancer

445
00:17:40,230 --> 00:17:41,690
is cellular atypia.

446
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:43,610
Why don't I take a step back?

447
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:47,370
Remember that endometrial hyperplasia is a pathologic hyperplasia.

448
00:17:48,050 --> 00:17:50,610
So endometrial hyperplasia is a risk factor

449
00:17:50,610 --> 00:17:53,730
for the eventual development of carcinoma.

450
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:54,930
So that's point one.

451
00:17:55,690 --> 00:17:58,530
Point two is when you have endometrial hyperplasia,

452
00:17:58,990 --> 00:18:01,450
then you need to remember that we want to ask

453
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:03,890
what's the risk of that endometrial hyperplasia

454
00:18:03,890 --> 00:18:05,530
in that patient going on to cancer.

455
00:18:05,950 --> 00:18:08,030
And the answer is that if we want to predict the risk,

456
00:18:08,130 --> 00:18:12,070
the risk is most dependent on the presence or absence of cellular atypia.

457
00:18:12,430 --> 00:18:13,930
So cellular atypia is key.

458
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:17,510
And this is something that we absolutely have to be familiar with.

459
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:20,870
Now, of course, the consequence of endometrial hyperplasia

460
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:22,250
is endometrial carcinoma.

461
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:25,210
So we want to now discuss endometrial carcinoma.

462
00:18:25,590 --> 00:18:26,870
What is endometrial carcinoma?

463
00:18:27,010 --> 00:18:29,770
A malignant proliferation of endometrial glands.

464
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,030
How is it going to present?

465
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:33,090
Well, you've got this growth of the endometrium,

466
00:18:33,170 --> 00:18:35,110
and as it begins to grow, eventually it'll bleed.

467
00:18:35,510 --> 00:18:38,230
And so the patients classically present with postmenopausal bleeding.

468
00:18:38,730 --> 00:18:41,790
Now, I'd like to remind you that there are two pathways

469
00:18:41,790 --> 00:18:43,390
for endometrial carcinoma.

470
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:45,850
So when we think about endometrial carcinoma,

471
00:18:45,850 --> 00:18:47,730
there are two distinct pathways.

472
00:18:48,310 --> 00:18:50,930
The first pathway is the hyperplasia pathway.

473
00:18:51,650 --> 00:18:54,370
And this makes sense based on our prior discussion.

474
00:18:54,810 --> 00:18:57,710
Patient has unopposed estrogen floating around in the blood.

475
00:18:58,110 --> 00:19:00,630
The unopposed estrogen hits the endometrium.

476
00:19:00,790 --> 00:19:03,870
The endometrium grows and grows and grows and grows

477
00:19:03,870 --> 00:19:05,370
and develops a hyperplasia.

478
00:19:05,730 --> 00:19:08,650
Eventually, that hyperplasia becomes carcinoma.

479
00:19:09,090 --> 00:19:11,930
And so this is an example of the hyperplasia carcinoma,

480
00:19:12,170 --> 00:19:14,490
pathologic hyperplasia carcinoma sequence.

481
00:19:14,490 --> 00:19:18,690
Now, what's important to note here is that when patients get this type of tumor,

482
00:19:19,010 --> 00:19:23,650
there's a classic histology, and the classic histology is called endometrioid.

483
00:19:24,290 --> 00:19:27,650
Endo, E-N-D-O, metrioid.

484
00:19:29,250 --> 00:19:30,330
All right, endometrioid.

485
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:36,090
Now, what we mean by endometrioid is that the cancer looks very much like the normal endometrium.

486
00:19:36,090 --> 00:19:38,690
So we call it endometrioid.

487
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:40,630
And again, so that's one pathway.

488
00:19:40,870 --> 00:19:44,270
Hyperplasia, pathologic hyperplasia due to unopposed estrogen,

489
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:46,150
which eventually results in carcinoma,

490
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:51,210
which the classic histology of which is the endometrioid histology.

491
00:19:51,570 --> 00:19:54,190
Now, the other pathway is called a sporadic pathway.

492
00:19:54,190 --> 00:19:59,680
And in the sporadic pathway, you don't have hyperplasia.

493
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:03,920
You get cancer from an atrophic endometrium.

494
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:06,740
Cancer from an atrophic endometrium.

495
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:09,520
There is no evident precursor lesion.

496
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:13,600
The endometrium is basically atrophic, and it develops into a cancer.

497
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:16,480
And what's important to note is that in this particular pathway,

498
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:18,920
the histology is something called serous.

499
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:26,740
All right, and serous histology often has the formation of papillae or papillary structures.

500
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:29,600
So we can also call it papillary serous.

501
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:32,100
And it might be easier to remember it that way

502
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,880
because there's going to be a high-yield association

503
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:36,980
that's going to come up concerning papillary serous in a moment.

504
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:39,780
Now, a few important things about the sporadic pathway.

505
00:20:40,220 --> 00:20:42,720
Number one, this usually occurs in the elderly.

506
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:45,260
So you're talking about a woman greater than the age of 70.

507
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:50,740
Whereas the hyperplasia pathway usually occurs in a woman about the age of 50, for example.

508
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,600
So that's one, you know, 50-60, for example.

509
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:56,420
That's one particular distinction that we'd like to make here.

510
00:20:56,780 --> 00:20:59,680
Another important distinction that I'd like to make is that the sporadic pathway

511
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:03,880
is driven by P53 mutations, very high-yield.

512
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:08,860
In the sporadic pathway, it's very common to find P53 mutations.

513
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:12,420
Now, with that background, you can now understand what I've written in the text.

514
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:13,960
So let's walk through the text together.

515
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:16,520
Endometrial carcinoma, as I've already stated,

516
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:19,000
is a malignant proliferation of endometrial glands.

517
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:20,160
It's going to present with bleeding.

518
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:22,080
And there's two distinct pathways.

519
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:26,240
In the hyperplastic pathway, you get carcinoma that comes from hyperplasia.

520
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:28,400
The risk factors are all based on estrogen.

521
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:30,160
The average age is about 50.

522
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:32,640
And the histology is endometrioid.

523
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:35,420
In the sporadic pathway, you have an atrophic endometrium

524
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:38,300
with no evident precursor lesion.

525
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,520
And the average age is about 70.

526
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:42,480
The histology, of course, will be serous.

527
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:44,940
And if I'd add one more thing here, which is in your book,

528
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,400
but I haven't written here on the slides, P53.

529
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:50,180
This pathway is driven by P53.

530
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:54,020
Finally, recall that I told you that in the serous pathway,

531
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:56,220
you often have the formation of papillae.

532
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:58,400
And so you get these finger-like growths.

533
00:21:58,660 --> 00:22:01,300
Now, it would not be uncommon for the finger-like growths

534
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:06,140
to eventually necrose and allow for calcification to occur on their surface.

535
00:22:06,620 --> 00:22:09,020
And so you can get something called somoma bodies,

536
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:12,480
which are concentrically layered calcifications

537
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:14,700
that will arise in this type of tumor.

538
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:18,020
And in particular, this tumor, one more thing to bear in mind,

539
00:22:18,220 --> 00:22:19,760
is particularly aggressive.

540
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,380
It has a very aggressive behavior.

541
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:26,620
Here's a gross of endometrial carcinoma.

542
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:29,080
Again, you're well aware that this is the cervix,

543
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:32,080
and now we've come into the uterine cavity.

544
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:38,120
And in the uterine cavity, it should normally be smooth and shiny the way it is here.

545
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:40,720
But there's clearly this growth right over here,

546
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:45,060
which represents, in this particular case, endometrial carcinoma.

547
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:49,080
Now, here would be a picture of the endometrioid histology,

548
00:22:49,260 --> 00:22:51,900
which we would see in the hyperplastic pathway.

549
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:54,780
And so this kind of looks like normal endometrium,

550
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:59,020
but it's all piled up on itself, and it's totally disorganized,

551
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:02,820
and it looks like there's really almost minimal stroma here.

552
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:09,520
And so this represents endometrial carcinoma, the endometrioid histology.

553
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:14,960
This is the sporadic pathway in which the patients develop a papillary serous histology most often.

554
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:17,660
And so here is the classic blood vessel,

555
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:20,200
and then you're getting these papillary projections,

556
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:22,860
and this is a papillary projection cut on end.

557
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:27,660
So these are the classic fibrovascular cores that you would find in a papillary projection.

558
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:32,500
Now, of course, one thing to note is that you can actually get death of this region

559
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:37,160
with concentric calcification, and that is called a somoma body,

560
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:39,540
and somoma bodies would be seen in this particular tumor.

561
00:23:39,980 --> 00:23:41,580
Just as a very brief global review,

562
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:45,220
can we remind ourselves in other cases where we might see somoma bodies?

563
00:23:45,220 --> 00:23:46,940
Just list for me the tumors.

564
00:23:48,580 --> 00:23:51,560
All right, so another example would be papillary carcinoma of the thyroid,

565
00:23:51,780 --> 00:23:56,940
where you have papillary configuration and subsequently could develop somoma bodies.

566
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:59,980
Another example would be meningioma.

567
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:04,080
Meningioma is another high-yield tumor in which patients get somoma bodies.

568
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:07,700
Another example would be this tumor, papillary serous carcinoma.

569
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:11,140
Whether it be of the endometrium, we can also form this tumor in the ovary.

570
00:24:11,420 --> 00:24:13,360
In both cases, we would get somoma bodies.

571
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:15,720
And there's one that students tend to forget,

572
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:18,420
but it's actually kind of high-yield for exams.

573
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:20,680
Mesothelioma.

574
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:24,000
In mesothelioma, which is a tumor of the pleura,

575
00:24:24,380 --> 00:24:26,380
remember classically related to asbestos,

576
00:24:26,860 --> 00:24:30,720
in mesothelioma, patients can also develop somoma bodies in that tumor.

577
00:24:30,980 --> 00:24:35,320
So that's one to be aware of, and that's actually kind of a high-yield point as well.

578
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:38,660
All right, so that clears up our discussion of endometrium,

579
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:40,060
and now we go to myometrium.

580
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:44,300
Remember that the myometrium is the smooth muscle that underlies the endometrium,

581
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:47,060
and there's only really two key things that we have to discuss.

582
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:51,780
The first is a tumor of the smooth muscle, which is benign, which is called leiomyoma.

583
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:53,720
Leiomyo, smooth muscle.

584
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:54,920
Oma, mass.

585
00:24:55,300 --> 00:24:59,020
So this is a mass of smooth muscle, and it will be benign.

586
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:02,360
It usually arises from the myometrium related to estrogen.

587
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:03,120
That's important.

588
00:25:10,060 --> 00:25:12,520
And they have estrogen floating around in their blood.

589
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:16,420
Another important point to note is that it's often multiple.

590
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:21,340
So usually you'll find multiple masses within the uterine wall.

591
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:23,540
They enlarge during pregnancy.

592
00:25:23,820 --> 00:25:26,660
That's another relation to estrogen exposure.

593
00:25:27,040 --> 00:25:28,800
And they tend to shrink after menopause.

594
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:31,280
Again, another relation to estrogen exposure.

595
00:25:31,860 --> 00:25:34,280
Now one of the things that drives students crazy is that,

596
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:35,780
you know, why do I have to know this?

597
00:25:35,780 --> 00:25:38,920
They are multiple well-defined white whirly masses.

598
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:42,520
And that actually is important, and I'll explain why in a minute.

599
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:46,780
But you do have to know that they are multiple well-defined white whirly masses.

600
00:25:47,380 --> 00:25:48,860
Now, here is what they look like.

601
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:51,240
This is basically the uterine cavity here.

602
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:57,140
You can see that I've got these large, sort of very distinct white whirly masses.

603
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:59,560
There's numerous here.

604
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:04,120
And this is the classic gross examination of leiomyomas.

605
00:26:04,120 --> 00:26:06,440
Now, why are we making such a big deal about the,

606
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:10,440
and why does it show up on exams all the time about this white whirly masses stuff?

607
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:17,040
Well, it's important because the first reason is important is because when you have multiple,

608
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:19,480
that usually indicates leiomyoma,

609
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:23,480
as opposed to the malignant version of this smooth muscle tumor,

610
00:26:23,580 --> 00:26:25,260
which is called leiomyosarcoma.

611
00:26:25,460 --> 00:26:29,640
So the fact that they're multiple is important because that usually indicates that it's benign.

612
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:32,840
It's more likely to be benign, the process that is.

613
00:26:32,840 --> 00:26:36,080
So that's one important point and why multiple becomes so important.

614
00:26:36,700 --> 00:26:42,800
The other reason why we talk about this white whirly stuff so much is because when you do the gross examination,

615
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:48,280
that's another important way by which you make a distinction between leiomyoma and the malignant variant,

616
00:26:48,460 --> 00:26:50,120
which is leiomyosarcoma.

617
00:26:50,120 --> 00:26:53,980
So if I see white whirly regular masses, that's benign.

618
00:26:54,300 --> 00:27:00,780
But if I see necrosis or hemorrhage or some irregularity in the gross examination of the tumor,

619
00:27:00,940 --> 00:27:06,780
it raises my worry that this perhaps is not leiomyoma, but instead leiomyosarcoma.

620
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:11,500
So two key distinctions between leiomyoma and leiomyosarcoma.

621
00:27:11,620 --> 00:27:13,080
Leiomyoma is usually multiple.

622
00:27:13,860 --> 00:27:16,320
Leiomyosarcoma is usually single.

623
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:20,820
Leiomyoma is usually white whirly regular masses.

624
00:27:21,360 --> 00:27:25,800
Leiomyosarcoma often has hemorrhage or necrosis in the center of the mass.

625
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,740
And if I was to make one third distinction,

626
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:32,040
leiomyoma, disease of premenopausal women driven by estrogen.

627
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:36,980
Leiomyosarcoma, the malignant variant, disease of postmenopausal women,

628
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:43,480
usually seen in women, you know, much older than, like, you know, 70, 80 years of age, for example.

629
00:27:43,820 --> 00:27:47,260
So this is some important distinctions to be aware of.

630
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:52,080
Now, another important point is that leiomyomas are usually asymptomatic.

631
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,580
It's a very common tumor.

632
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:57,080
Many, many women have this tumor, but it's usually asymptomatic.

633
00:27:57,620 --> 00:27:59,720
Believe it or not, they like to ask this on exams.

634
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:04,080
So the most common clinical finding in a patient with leiomyoma would be nothing.

635
00:28:04,280 --> 00:28:05,560
They're not going to present with symptoms.

636
00:28:06,080 --> 00:28:07,940
However, if they do have symptoms,

637
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:11,920
the symptoms will be a derivative of the fact that they have leiomyomas.

638
00:28:12,040 --> 00:28:14,740
For example, one thing that the leiomyomas can do,

639
00:28:14,820 --> 00:28:16,420
they can stretch the endometrial lining,

640
00:28:16,520 --> 00:28:18,840
and when they stretch the endometrial lining, the patient will bleed.

641
00:28:19,420 --> 00:28:21,140
Another thing that the leiomyomas can do,

642
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:26,540
they can block the ability of the fertilized ovum to actually implant within the wall

643
00:28:26,540 --> 00:28:28,760
because of the distortion of the uterine cavity.

644
00:28:28,760 --> 00:28:30,560
So that could result in infertility.

645
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:34,780
Of course, the leiomyomas produce a mass within the uterine wall,

646
00:28:34,900 --> 00:28:37,520
and so that could result in a pelvic mass.

647
00:28:37,780 --> 00:28:40,580
So the symptoms are very straightforward if you understand the tumor,

648
00:28:41,020 --> 00:28:44,140
but what's important to note is that this is usually asymptomatic.

649
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:47,600
Okay, leiomyosarcoma I've kind of touched on already.

650
00:28:48,320 --> 00:28:50,080
Leiomyo refers to smooth muscle,

651
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:53,600
and then sarcoma means malignant mesenchymal proliferation.

652
00:28:53,600 --> 00:28:57,540
So it is a malignant mesenchymal proliferation of smooth muscle

653
00:28:57,540 --> 00:28:59,720
that classically arises from the myometrium.

654
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:03,020
High yield point number one arises de novo.

655
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:07,780
Leomyomas do not become leiomyosarcoma.

656
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:11,600
Again, leiomyoma does not become leiomyosarcoma.

657
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:16,560
Leomyosarcoma is a completely separate tumor that arises de novo.

658
00:29:16,780 --> 00:29:18,320
It arises on its own.

659
00:29:18,580 --> 00:29:19,880
That's high yield point number one.

660
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:24,820
High yield point number two is that this is usually seen in postmenopausal women.

661
00:29:25,360 --> 00:29:29,100
Now, remember that leiomyoma is a disease of premenopausal women,

662
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:31,960
and in fact, leiomyomas usually go away after menopause

663
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:33,460
because they were dependent on estrogen,

664
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:35,660
and when the estrogen is gone, they will shrink.

665
00:29:36,020 --> 00:29:40,660
However, leiomyosarcoma is usually seen in postmenopausal women.

666
00:29:40,900 --> 00:29:42,160
So that's point number two.

667
00:29:42,940 --> 00:29:45,060
High yield point number three is that leiomyosarcoma

668
00:29:45,060 --> 00:29:48,240
is usually a single lesion with necrosis and hemorrhage,

669
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:52,480
whereas leiomyoma is multiple white whirly masses.

670
00:29:53,020 --> 00:29:55,160
Leiomyoma, multiple white whirly masses.

671
00:29:55,720 --> 00:30:00,700
Leiomyosarcoma, signal lesion with necrosis and hemorrhage on gross examination.

672
00:30:01,340 --> 00:30:02,240
And when I look at these histologically,

673
00:30:02,980 --> 00:30:07,020
the key finding is going to be that I'm going to see necrosis histologically,

674
00:30:08,060 --> 00:30:11,020
I'm going to see mitotic activity, and cellular atypia.

675
00:30:11,020 --> 00:30:16,200
But again, my assessment and my distinction between whether I'm dealing with a leiomyoma

676
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:19,240
or a leiomyosarcoma starts with gross examination.

677
00:30:19,360 --> 00:30:21,000
I would say that's the highest yield,

678
00:30:21,260 --> 00:30:25,200
to recognize that leiomyosarcoma will be a single lesion with necrosis and hemorrhage,

679
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:29,880
and then when I do the histology, I will see necrosis, atypia,

680
00:30:30,040 --> 00:30:32,080
which would be classic for a malignant lesion,

681
00:30:32,340 --> 00:30:36,900
and increased mitotic activity, which would also be classic for a malignant lesion.

682
00:30:36,900 --> 00:30:39,960
So once you've understood leiomyoma and leiomyosarcoma,

683
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:41,940
that closes off this particular section.

684
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:44,660
And our next discussion is going to be the ovary.

